note('Seed-0 RNG offsets work across all 168 factors; initializer residuals RMS 1.3e−4–4.6e−4. Learned ΔA_g and ΔA_u have a matching top input axis (cos ~0.73–0.92 over blocks 8–18), independently confirming sign +570, −208, −262 and late +490. Initialized sketches of these mass coordinates have ~0.8–0.94 cosine with the signed dominant B phase selected by ΔA. Thus the earlier ordinary-token prior is broadly real; ΔA itself is per-coordinate standardized by Adam, not an activation mean. ΔA-weighted left outputs in blocks 12–15 corroborate the same cross-module clinical axis. Late O on value bias has ~2–5 residual units before sink masking; B ΔA on that same bias often partly cancels the larger B A_init term (1–10%).')